Tor 0.4.6.10 — PREMATURE_DATA real-attack patch (env-gated, benign by default)
File: src/core/or/circuitbuild.c  (modified-client / fault-injection model, same
spirit as CREATE_FLOOD and CIRCUIT_HIJACK)

GOAL
  Produce a GENUINE RELAY_BEGIN cell on the wire while the circuit's FSM is still
  in CIRCUIT_BUILDING (i.e. before the circuit is READY). The harness keys
  PREMATURE_DATA off the real connection_ap_handshake_send_begin() info-log; that
  log is emitted only from inside the real function, so we call the real function
  (no fabricated log line).

WHY THIS IS THE ONLY GENUINE PATH
  A stock Tor client NEVER emits premature data: connection_ap_handshake_send_begin
  is reached only via connection_ap_handshake_attach_chosen_circuit, which asserts
  circ->base_.state == CIRCUIT_STATE_OPEN; and connection_ap_supports_optimistic_data
  returns 0 unless the circuit is OPEN. So the only way to get a real begin cell
  during BUILDING is a modified (malicious) client that links a waiting stream to
  the first (already-OPEN) hop and sends the begin early. The cell is real; the
  relay (a middle node) will reject/END the stream, the circuit survives.

HOOK (circuit_finish_handshake, right after CIRC_EVENT_EXTENDED for the FIRST hop)
  At that point circ->cpath (hop 1) is CPATH_STATE_OPEN and the circuit is BUILDING.
  We grab one AP stream in AP_CONN_STATE_CIRCUIT_WAIT, link it to circ at the first
  hop (replicating link_apconn_to_circ inline because that fn is static in
  circuituse.c; passing cpath=circ->cpath avoids the OPEN-state assert), and call
  connection_ap_handshake_send_begin(ec).

SAFETY
  - assert_circ_anonymity_ok (in send_begin) only asserts when build_state->
    onehop_tunnel is set; normal 3-hop general circuits skip it -> no abort.
  - We filter SOCKS_COMMAND_IS_CONNECT and require !on_circuit, so we never hijack
    a RESOLVE stream (would trip send_begin's SOCKS_COMMAND_IS_CONNECT assert) and
    never double-link a stream.
  - Fires once per circuit (first hop). Benign by default (env unset => no-op).

--- a/src/core/or/circuitbuild.c (includes)
+++ b/src/core/or/circuitbuild.c
@@
 #include "core/or/entry_connection_st.h"
+#include "core/or/socks_request_st.h"

--- a/src/core/or/circuitbuild.c (circuit_finish_handshake)
+++ b/src/core/or/circuitbuild.c
@@
   circuit_event_status(circ, CIRC_EVENT_EXTENDED, 0);
+
+  if (hop == circ->cpath && getenv("TOR_FSM_ATTACK_PREMATURE_DATA")) {
+    connection_t *pc = connection_get_by_type_state(CONN_TYPE_AP, AP_CONN_STATE_CIRCUIT_WAIT);
+    if (pc) {
+      entry_connection_t *ec = TO_ENTRY_CONN(pc);
+      if (ec->socks_request && SOCKS_COMMAND_IS_CONNECT(ec->socks_request->command) && !ENTRY_TO_EDGE_CONN(ec)->on_circuit) {
+        ENTRY_TO_EDGE_CONN(ec)->next_stream = circ->p_streams;
+        ENTRY_TO_EDGE_CONN(ec)->on_circuit = TO_CIRCUIT(circ);
+        circ->p_streams = ENTRY_TO_EDGE_CONN(ec);
+        ENTRY_TO_EDGE_CONN(ec)->cpath_layer = circ->cpath;
+        (void) connection_ap_handshake_send_begin(ec);
+      }
+    }
+  }
+
   /* (CIRCUIT_HIJACK block, if applied, follows here) */
   return 0;
 }
